course: dictionary
lesson: 3185
title: Encourage: hope and support
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To encourage someone is to give them hope, confidence or support so they keep trying. «Teachers and friends encourage each other: "You can do it!" and "Keep going!"» Those words are the clues. Each one helps someone try again.
explain: Encourage can also mean to help something happen or grow. In science, sunlight and water encourage plants to grow. Good habits encourage health. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try "help" in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Ada, the daughter of the poet Lord Byron, was encouraged by her mother to study maths. «Her mother encouraged her to study maths» means her mother gave her support so she kept learning. Encouraging, encouraged and encourages are all forms of the same verb.
fact: Encourage means to give someone hope, confidence or support so they keep trying.
fact: Encourage can also mean to help something happen or grow, like sunlight encouraging plants.
fact: «Encouraging words» are kind words that give someone the courage to keep going.
fact: Encourage is a verb: encourage, encourages, encouraged, encouraging.
fact: Ada's mother encouraged her to study maths, and Ada called her approach "poetical science".
exercise: «Teachers do much more than explain facts: they care, notice and encourage.» What does encourage mean here? | *To give pupils hope and support so they keep trying | To shout loudly at the class | To explain facts only | To cancel lessons
exercise: «Sunlight and water encourage plants to grow.» Which word best replaces encourage? | sleep | ignore | stop | *help
exercise: A coach shouts, «Keep going, you're getting better!» What is the coach doing? | Ending the match | Sleeping | *Encouraging the team | Ignoring the team
test: «Her mother encouraged her to study maths.» Which word means helped and supported her to keep learning? | maths | poet | *encouraged | daughter
test: Which is an example of encouraging words? | «Stop, that's wrong.» | «I don't care what you do.» | *«Keep going, you can do it!» | «Sit down and be quiet.»
exam: Teachers do more than explain facts: they care, notice and ____ pupils. | punish | ignore | *encourage | forget
